#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186363851 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4feb6eca-9baf-537a-bd96-4e75951c9f35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363853} {:answer/id #uuid "861fc691-bc44-5884-aa45-fe3dda66296d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "861fc691-bc44-5884-aa45-fe3dda66296d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363854} :answer-field/id #uuid "61833109-c1bc-500b-ac07-6456a7f484a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186363852}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5e37ea72-4527-59b0-9b76-eb7bab82018e" :question/math-academy-id "q-316602" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14069841/assets/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-8)\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 3=-40.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-40\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =40.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186092846 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51f9b53-0ce5-518f-8173-abe4d87f2851" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c0c700c-05d2-5fac-8132-0ca5c0d0d99d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091542} {:answer/id #uuid "eda936fe-a392-588b-beeb-c230c8ace582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091543} {:answer/id #uuid "020589a6-8200-5bbb-afd3-ce4a0a234460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091544} {:answer/id #uuid "27611fb5-040d-5c37-a5b1-b0c7d01f2a50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091545} {:answer/id #uuid "60970469-1ad7-5044-9bd9-e511d49415cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091546}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eda936fe-a392-588b-beeb-c230c8ace582" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091543} :answer-field/id #uuid "5217ad8c-045f-5d11-98dc-a3527d677598" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186091541}] :question/id #uuid "34fb5c40-9873-55cf-a77d-c4a2ec2ac3ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-9297" :question/problem "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1, 0), (0, 0), (0, 1), (1, 1)$. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T$, given below?\n\n$T = \\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186303300 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4d59733f-3396-5d59-98a9-3f2e0ccfbbc4" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area of the Image of an Object Under a Linear Transformation Given a Diagram"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63131879-2b6e-5b83-83dd-a031a832723b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303302} {:answer/id #uuid "300a3c35-9bdc-526e-a0e2-a3e1c6d3da61" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303303} {:answer/id #uuid "b1a00c06-8cc0-5ba1-9c02-5af4e0877c33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303304} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff9ee8f-390b-513b-9a00-66b2db1dd708" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "23" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303305} {:answer/id #uuid "bf97bd72-0294-51d9-9663-7987a2190c25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303306}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b1a00c06-8cc0-5ba1-9c02-5af4e0877c33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303304} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1d90599-afa5-593e-84e0-cb850f9e6efe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c827fba0-90ed-5026-9ebc-6dd1e8034231" :question/math-academy-id "q-9309" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039564/assets/bd50e99a129b1d6a2c6b73145dbf68681bc92a3cef0ca8e743b63cf96c9afafc.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot (2+4)=6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=2\\cdot 3-5\\cdot (-1)=11.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,11\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
